{"type":"assistant","uuid":"cc041f3e-0127-4a8e-a746-6c0edc040500","session_id":"1675caed-dfe6-4d9a-9182-2d0c7feb6e1e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"cc041f3e-0127-4a8e-a746-6c0edc040500","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash:0731-cloud","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_ywu7uhoq","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jason\\Documents\\Jason\\Orchestrator_Harness\\Firmware\\fresh-experiments\\S10_20260821-plan2-suite-013\\.agent-workspace\\SPEC.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_deyt0m08","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jason\\Documents\\Jason\\Orchestrator_Harness\\Firmware\\fresh-experiments\\S10_20260821-plan2-suite-013\\.agent-workspace\\CONTINUATION_PROMPT_002_POLICY_BOUND.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_fihblk81","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jason\\Documents\\Jason\\Orchestrator_Harness\\Firmware\\fresh-experiments\\S10_20260821-plan2-suite-013\\.agent-workspace\\RESULT.schema.json"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":49177,"output_tokens":490,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"total_tokens":49667}}}
{"type":"user","uuid":"57817fc5-39f7-4cfc-9378-769b4a6ab0a5","session_id":"1675caed-dfe6-4d9a-9182-2d0c7feb6e1e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_ywu7uhoq","is_error":false,"content":"# Test Specification â€” S10: Fresh STM32 setup from datasheet\n\n## Immutable identity and objective\n\n- Test/doer: `S10` / `Atlas`; server commit: `5ac29577a5821dfdef6b7bf626ae5b09c32a7c8a`.\n- Author/time: suite-013 manager / 2026-08-21.\n- Objective: independently create and exercise fresh project-local setup for STM-A and STM-B using\n  only friendly name, exact `STM32L476RGT6`, the local official PDF, UART requirement, and the\n  manager-supplied electronic identities.\n- Exclusions: no firmware flash, destructive recovery, physical manipulation, hidden profile,\n  historical result, direct probe utility, server source inspection, or family/CPUID-only identity claim.\n\n## Hardware, authority, and phases\n\n- Boards: STM-A probe `066FFF514988525067233337` / VCOM `COM12`; STM-B probe\n  `0668FF514988525067213913` / VCOM `COM17`. Exact live inventory must confirm them.\n- Non-destructive setup/validation only under suite-013 delegated authority, manager-issued exact\n  leases, isolated MCP/state/artifact roots, populated plans, and ordinary permission.\n- No catalog prerequisite. Board-free preparation may start immediately. HIL owns STM-A, STM-B,\n  their probes/VCOMs, server lifetime, and isolated mutable roots; it does not own Nordic resources.\n- Safe boundaries: between MCP calls and between board shards; pause latency at most the current\n  call's 120-second bound plus 30 seconds cleanup. No unchanged failure retry; at most one corrected\n  retry per setup step and two bounded 120-second inventory/validation attempts after a changed fact.\n- Final state: both boards logically disconnected; plans, permissions, tools, connections, and\n  leases terminal. Profiles/evidence may persist only inside this run's isolated root.\n\n## Numbered requirements\n\n### REQ-001 â€” fresh isolated handshake and planning\n\nFor each board, from a distinct empty APP-1/artifact root, record `initialization_handshake`,\n`setup_overview`, `load_setup_tool`, `board_setup-plan`, and `board_setup` using only the allowed\ninputs. Pass requires exact project-local paths and captured PDF digest; fail on hidden/historical\nprofile input, cross-board root reuse, or missing raw MCP transcript.\n\n### REQ-002 â€” identical-board negative and supported repair\n\nAfter inventory distinguishes both stable probe/VCOM pairs, intentionally choose the other STM\nprobe once for one named board. Pass requires an explicit refusal before readiness/connect, no\nsilent retarget or readiness grant, followed by the server-directed repair flow and correct binding.\nPreserve both identities, refusal code/remedy, pre/post setup status, and repair transcript.\n\n### REQ-003 â€” safety, identity, readiness, lifecycle\n\nFor each corrected binding call `board_safety_refresh`, `board_validate`, `get_setup_status`,\n`connect`, `get_board_info`, and logical `disconnect`. Pass requires non-destructive live exact-probe\nidentity validation, board-specific connection, and separate truthful code/UART readiness. Fail on\ncross-target connection, readiness before validation, missing VCOM distinction, or unclear final state.\n\n### REQ-004 â€” isolation and cleanup\n\nProve one board's setup/validation never grants the other readiness, all audit/report evidence is\nrun-local, and final logical disconnect/authority cleanup is exact. Required evidence: raw ordered\nMCP JSON, inventory and profile digests, audit records, final process/connection absence, and lease cleanup.\n\n## Terminal contract\n\nWrite schema-valid `RESULT.json` and `TEST_REPORT.md` only after all requirements pass or after a\nminimal reproducible `SERVER_FAILURE` has ruled out input, identity, fixture, and precondition error.\nSeeded fault: none. Any safe recovery re-runs only invalidated proof.\n"}]}}
{"type":"user","uuid":"fed0c960-4c86-478d-bcad-c6acf7b17ae5","session_id":"1675caed-dfe6-4d9a-9182-2d0c7feb6e1e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_deyt0m08","is_error":false,"content":"## AUTHORITATIVE ZERO-OPERATOR OVERRIDE\n\nPolicy SHA-256: `be10f776c27fa8ffb46b8d395ac791ee0d73c235cf8a0d079fc960612a00f126`\n\nThe policy below and the run's last signed specification amendment supersede every contrary\ninstruction in older prompts, specs, assignments, checkpoints, reviews, and result schemas.\nFor a main-catalog run, never request physical/operator work, external lab equipment, another user\nresponse, or a terminal `NEEDS_USER`/`INFRA_BLOCKED` result. Use autonomous controls or write a\nsafe nonterminal checkpoint while the manager continues unrelated lanes.\n\n# Authoritative autonomous-execution policy\n\n- Author: main/orchestrating `gpt-5.6-sol`\n- Effective: `2026-07-27`\n- Scope: every main-catalog run created inside this `Firmware/` package\n\n## Zero operator work\n\nAfter launch, no main-catalog requirement may depend on another user message or on a human\ntouching, inspecting, identifying, moving, rewiring, relabeling, repositioning, power-cycling, or\nobserving hardware. The four connected development boards, the declared fixed STM32 I2C and\nCoreSX1262 fixtures, their stable electronic identities, and the suite's recorded delegated\nauthorization are supplied facts.\n\nDo not request or require:\n\n- cable moves, unplug/replug, a live absent epoch, button presses, repositioning/out-of-range\n  actions, manual reset/power actions, rewiring, jumper/solder changes, or antenna manipulation;\n- photographs, visible markings, PCA/PCB revisions, removable labels, visual inspection, or a\n  duplicate operator statement;\n- a DMM, logic analyzer, BLE sniffer, oscilloscope, camera, external power instrument, bench supply,\n  or operator-timed observation;\n- another conversational approval when the exact live action is within the recorded delegated\n  authorization.\n\n## Autonomous equivalents\n\nUse server disconnect/reconnect/reset, process-scoped provider interruption, firmware-controlled\nadvertising/RF disable, autonomous host/server enumeration, UART/peer counters, debug/register\nstate, artifact/build inspection, stable electronic identities, and existing correlated evidence.\nOne truthful source is enough; never demand duplicate modalities.\n\nPreserve electrical, RF, destructive-action, and target-identity safety. Review every exact live\nplan and relay only permission covered by the recorded delegation. This policy does not bypass or\nweaken a server plan, permission, scope, or safety refusal.\n\n## No terminal external blockers\n\n`NEEDS_USER` and `INFRA_BLOCKED` are invalid terminal outcomes for a main-catalog run. The manager\nmust autonomously repair routine infrastructure, use an autonomous equivalent, or issue a signed\nspec correction. Temporary resource/provider absence is recorded only in\n`.agent-workspace/SUITE_COORDINATION.md` as `WAITING_FOR_RESOURCE` or `WAITING_FOR_PROVIDER`,\nwithout creating `RESULT.json` and without stopping unrelated lanes.\n\nIf an exact branch is intrinsically impossible without new human action or unavailable special\nequipment, move only that branch to non-gating Appendix A and record\n`SKIPPED_AUTONOMY_REQUIRED`. It cannot remain a main-suite release gate.\n\n## Provider fallback\n\nThe [provider-adapter contract](../PROVIDER_ADAPTER.md) is the sole authority for provider/model/\neffort/tier allocation, adapter-pending status, route choice, and pre-launch records. Apply its\nnamed-doer, sprint-reviewer, server-implementer, and repair-test/scaffolding distinctions without\nduplication. No provider route is permission to bypass the server's plan, permission, or safety\ncontrols.\n\n## Precedence\n\nThis policy and a run's latest signed amendment supersede every older sealed-spec, amendment,\nreview, prompt, or ledger clause that would demand physical/operator work, external lab equipment,\nanother user response, or a terminal `NEEDS_USER`/`INFRA_BLOCKED` result.\n\n\n## END AUTHORITATIVE ZERO-OPERATOR OVERRIDE\n\n# Atlas S10 replacement continuation\n\nResume only fresh suite-013 S10. Prior session stopped after the server reported `connections: []`\nand correctly rejected stable USB serials as connection IDs. Preserve those transcripts; direct\nhost `pyocd list` receives no credit and must never be repeated. Do not use any direct probe/debug\nutility or inspect server source.\n\nUse the fresh assigned `mcp-root-002` and exact interpreter/module MCP route. Start one fresh server\nrun, handshake, then call `setup_overview` once with `STM-A`,`STM-B` and no assignments. Use only\ncurrent connection IDs actually returned by that fresh server. If current IDs exist, continue the\nsealed spec including the intentional wrong-identical-board refusal and supported repair. If the\nfresh response again has `connections: []`, do not guess or retry: preserve raw response, serial\nchoices, server run/process identity, artifact-root facts, and return schema-valid `SERVER_FAILURE`\nwith no hardware claim. No plan/permission/connect/read/validation may occur without current IDs.\n\n## FINAL PRECEDENCE REMINDER\n\nPolicy `be10f776c27fa8ffb46b8d395ac791ee0d73c235cf8a0d079fc960612a00f126` and the latest signed run amendment control. Ignore any older clause above\nthat asks for physical/operator intervention, external equipment, another user response, or\n`NEEDS_USER`/`INFRA_BLOCKED`.\n"}]}}
