h the exact MCP route (mcp-root-002)\n4. Handshake\n5. Call `setup_overview` once with `STM-A`, `STM-B` and no assignments\n6. If current IDs exist, continue the sealed spec\n7. If `connections: []` again, preserve evidence and return schema-valid `SERVER_FAILURE`\n\nWait â€” but I need to think about how the MCP server is launched. The controller status shows the MCP config used by the previous session:\n- command: `C:\\Users\\Jason\\Documents\\Jason\\Orchestrator_Harness\\Firmware\\BYO-Firmware-MCP\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe`\n- args: `[\"-m\", \"pyocd_debug_mcp.server\"]`\n- cwd: `C:\\Users\\Jason\\Documents\\Jason\\Orchestrator_Harness\\Firmware`\n- env: `BYO_MCP_ARTIFACT_ROOT` = `.agent-workspace\\mcp-root-002`\n\nIn my current session, the MCP server `byo-firmware` is already configured (I can see the mcp__byo-firmware__* tools available). The question is whether the currently configured MCP server in THIS session points to the right artifact root. Let me check what MCP servers are configured in this session.\n\nActually, I have the `mcp__byo-firmware__*` tools available in my toolset. The question is whether this session's MCP config matches the required route (mcp-root-002). Let me check the current session's MCP configuration. I should look at the settings or check what's configured.\n\nActually, the continuation prompt says \"Use the fresh assigned `mcp-root-002` and exact interpreter/module MCP route. Start one fresh server run, handshake, then call `setup_overview` once with `STM-A`,`STM-B` and no assignments.\"\n\nThe MCP server is launched by the client (qwen-code) with the mcp-config. In this session, I need to verify the MCP server is configured with the right artifact root. Let me check the current session's MCP configuration. I can check `.qwen/settings.json` or the session config.\n\nLet me first check the current state:\n1. Verify cwd\n2. Check whether mcp-root-002 exists\n3. Check the MCP server configuration for this session\n4. Check if there's a running MCP server process\n\nLet me look at the prior session's transcript tail to see exactly what happened (the `connections: []` response), and check the stderr log.\n\nActually, the continuation prompt says \"Preserve those transcripts\" â€” I should not delete them, but I can read them to understand the state. Let me check the tail of the replacement_002 codex jsonl to see the last state.\n\nLet me also check the current MCP server configuration. The tools available to me include `mcp__byo-firmware__*` â€” so the MCP server is configured in this session. I need to verify it points to mcp-root-002.\n\nLet me check:\n1. The current working directory\n2. Whether mcp-root-002 exists\n3. The MCP config in this session (maybe in .qwen/settings.json or the session config)\n4. The prior transcript tail\n\nLet me start.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
